---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro'
import { REPO } from '../data/site'

/** Bump when the policy text changes — not when the page is merely rebuilt. */
const UPDATED = '7 August 2026'

const title = 'Privacy — ReshapedPDF'
const description =
  'What ReshapedPDF does with your documents: nothing. No accounts, no telemetry, no uploads. The short, specific version.'
---
<Base title={title} description={description} width="narrow">
  <header class="slim"><div class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="/"><Mark size={19} /></a></div></header>

  <div class="wrap">
  
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="sub">The short version, because there is not much to say.</p>
  
    <div class="box">
      <b>ReshapedPDF has no servers.</b> There is no account to create, no telemetry, no crash
      reporting, no analytics, and no upload. Your documents are opened, edited and saved on your
      own machine. We could not read them if we wanted to, because they are never sent anywhere.
    </div>
  
    <h2>The desktop app</h2>
    <p>
      Everything happens locally. The app makes no network request of its own — not on launch, not
      on export, not ever — with the three exceptions below, each of which you start deliberately.
    </p>
  
    <h2>The web app</h2>
    <p>
      The browser version is the same code, served as static files. Your PDF is read by the browser
      itself and never leaves the tab; there is no upload endpoint to send it to. Closing the tab
      discards everything.
    </p>
  
    <h2>The three times anything leaves your machine</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>An AI model you connect.</b> The AI tools are bring-your-own-model. If you point the app
        at a local model (Ollama, LM Studio) nothing leaves your machine at all. If you point it at
        a hosted API with your own key, then the crop of the page you are working on is sent to
        <em>that provider</em>, under your agreement with them — never through us. The endpoint is
        whatever you typed in, and you can see it in the AI panel at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Checking for a new version, if you ask it to.</b> Release downloads are hosted on GitHub;
        opening that page is an ordinary visit to GitHub and subject to their privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>The list of models, when you open the Ollama setup panel.</b> It fetches the public
        catalogue of vision models from <code>ollama.com</code> so it can show you what is worth
        installing and how big each one is. No part of your document is involved — it is the same
        page anyone can open in a browser — and the panel says <em>live from ollama.com</em> above
        the list, so it is never happening invisibly. The result is cached on your device for a day.
        Pick any other provider and this request is not made at all.
      </li>
    </ul>
  
    <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Local browser/app storage keeps only your own preferences: the theme, your saved signature,
      the AI endpoint and model name you entered, and the cached Ollama model list. An API key you type is kept on your device so
      you do not have to retype it. None of it is transmitted. Clearing site data (web) or deleting
      the app's support folder (desktop) removes all of it.
    </p>
  
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      Static pages. No cookies, no trackers, no analytics scripts, no embedded third parties — the
      typefaces are served from this domain rather than from a font CDN, precisely so that visiting
      this page does not tell anyone else that you did. Your host will keep ordinary server logs.
    </p>
  
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Since no personal data is collected, there is nothing for us to export, correct or delete. If
      you believe otherwise, or you have any question about the above, write to
      <a href="mailto:anton.arnaudov.pro@gmail.com">anton.arnaudov.pro@gmail.com</a> and you will get a real answer.
    </p>
  
    
  </div>
  <div class="wrap"><footer>
    ReshapedPDF · <a href="/">Home</a> · <a href={REPO}>Source</a>
    {/* The date is the point of a privacy page's footer: it is how a reader
        knows which version of the policy they agreed to. It sits in `updated`
        so there is one place to change it. */}
    <div class="updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</div>
  </footer></div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  body.page-narrow a{color:var(--ember)}
  header.slim{border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair);padding:20px 0}
  header.slim .brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-family:var(--disp);font-size:19px;font-weight:640;color:var(--ink-bright);text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:-.02em}
  body.page-narrow h1{font-family:var(--disp);font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,44px);color:var(--ink-bright);letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.1;margin:56px 0 6px}
  body.page-narrow .sub{color:var(--dim);font-size:17px;margin-bottom:44px}
  body.page-narrow h2{font-family:var(--disp);font-size:21px;color:var(--ink-bright);font-weight:640;margin:38px 0 10px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  body.page-narrow p,body.page-narrow li{font-size:16px}
  body.page-narrow ul{margin:10px 0 0 20px}
  body.page-narrow li{margin:7px 0}
  body.page-narrow code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13.5px;background:var(--raised);border:1px solid var(--hair);border-radius:5px;padding:2px 6px;color:var(--ink-bright)}
  body.page-narrow .box{margin:26px 0;padding:22px 24px;border:1px solid var(--hair-strong);border-radius:13px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,92,31,.05),transparent)}
  body.page-narrow .box b{color:var(--ink-bright)}
  body.page-narrow footer{margin:72px 0 60px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--hair);color:var(--faint);font-size:13.5px}
  body.page-narrow .updated{color:var(--faint);font-size:13.5px;margin-top:8px}
</style>
